# ReviewNatin design & skills

## Required skills (read before UI work)

When building or styling **mobile** (`apps/mobile`):

- `building-native-ui` (~/.agents/skills/) — Expo Router, ScrollView + safe areas, components outside `app/`, kebab-case files
- `native-data-fetching` — Supabase via `lib/api/`, no axios
- `mobile-ux-patterns` — 48dp touch targets, max 3–4 nav depth, empty states with CTA
- `mobile-design-system` — spacing, hierarchy, Filipino-first copy

When building **marketing/admin web**:

- `frontend-design` (~/.claude/skills/) — distinctive layout, not generic purple-gradient SaaS

## Brand (do not drift)

- **Tone:** Filipino reviewer app — warm, clear Taglish where helpful, trustworthy (CSC/PRC disclaimers)
- **Colors:** `apps/mobile/constants/theme.ts` — primary `#1E4FD9`, accent `#F5B800`, light surfaces
- **Avoid AI slop:** no Inter/Roboto-only stacks, no purple-on-white hero clichés, no cookie-cutter card grids
- **Mobile:** PasaPath card is the hero CTA; readiness ring + streak; exam countdown in header

## Expo constraints

- Target **Expo SDK 56** with Expo Go from https://expo.dev/go (not Play Store SDK 54)
- Never run `npm audit fix --force` in this monorepo

## Code layout

- Routes: `apps/mobile/app/`
- UI + logic: `apps/mobile/components/`, `lib/`, `providers/`
- Shared exam slugs: `@reviewnatin/shared`
